# Build context is ~/Development/Pytinc (the parent), so these patterns are
# written to match at any depth across all three copied repos.

# VCS and editor noise
**/.git
**/.github
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/.DS_Store

# Virtualenvs and caches -- these are host-specific (host Python is 3.14, the
# image is 3.13) and would break `uv sync` if they leaked in.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
**/.uv
**/.uv_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage

# Build output
**/build
**/dist

# Secrets. Credentials reach the container through `podman run --env-file`,
# never baked into a layer -- an image layer is forever, and this image is not
# something you want to push anywhere with keys in it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
**/secrets.toml

# Local databases -- the container gets its own on the /data volume.
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.sqlite3-*

# Prebuilt dev wheels. Deliberately excluded: the image builds its own from the
# widgetset source it actually copied in, so the asset manifest always matches.
# (This is the one exclusion the old .dockerignore got right for the wrong
# reason -- it excluded the wheel but never rebuilt one, so the image shipped
# with no widgetset at all.)
**/wapyt-*-py3-none-any.whl

# Node, if the frontend build tooling is ever used from a checkout
**/node_modules

# Large vendored pieces that are NOT excludable: pytincture/frontend/pyodide is
# 12 MB and is served to the browser at runtime. Do not add it here.
